From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: serlk <22211586+Serlk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 13:19:21 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 21/21] media: mediatek: camraw: Load the start request before
 the first frame

With the earlier stream-on order the timing generator overran on the
first line of the first frame and RAW-B never loaded a register: the
double buffer toggle came before the start request ran, so the values
its lists wrote reached the working copy of RAW-A only at the first
start of frame, too late for the readers that prefetch, and never on
RAW-B, which has no timing generator to load them.

Stream on now follows the order of the captured stream: reset both
engines; per engine the camsys settings (ready/request snapshot set-up
on RAW, YUV and RMS, CQ reader FIFO thresholds, halt words, low latency
off, the engine's urgent pair); initialize both; the start request on
RAW-A, waiting for both done bits; sensor interface and sensor; then the
double buffer toggle and WFBC_INC := WFBC_EN on RAW and YUV of every
engine; then on RAW-A the start period, the done tolerance, the
DB_LOAD_DIS pulse and the viewfinder. Per frame only the lists are
started on RAW-A. db_order=1 keeps the earlier order. With this both RAW
engines run and frames are delivered (1450x1088 on a lit scene).

Also by default now: cam-sel at 312 MHz while streaming, the error
report masks at port base + 0x34, and a picture delivered at
SW_PASS1_DONE (frame_done=1 keeps the next start of frame).

Diagnostics: selection, writer enable, misc and WFBC words of each
engine before the viewfinder and at stop; at the first error the
ready/request words of RAW, YUV and RMS; the timing generator's measured
size and state and the INT3/INT8 done and underflow bits by name; the
larb ports of each engine at probe.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
